{
  "netclass": "bench-wire",
  "label": "Bench wiring",
  "permitted_rise_c": 30,
  "placement": "external",
  "note": {
    "en": "Loose wire in free air, which is what everything on a bench is. It states no copper weight, and the absence is the point: wire is round and is sold by cross-section, so asking this class for a trace width is asking a question about a board that is not being built. Thirty degrees is the rise the AWG chassis-wiring tables are drawn at, which is why an AWG 24 lead is rated 3.5 A there and a great deal less on a board."
  }
}
